# The website build only needs web/ (its Root Directory is set to "web" in
# Vercel's project settings). Deploying from the monorepo root is required —
# Vercel resolves Root Directory against the uploaded tree — but the CLI does
# not reliably honor nested .gitignore rules for the upload step, so a
# gitignored-but-present scratch file (outputs/leads/.../vectors.json, 131MB)
# blew Vercel's 100MB per-file upload cap. Excluding every non-web top-level
# directory explicitly, same intent as .dockerignore.
#
# MUST STAY: .git and scripts/ — web/vercel.json's ignoreCommand runs
# `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` and `bash scripts/vercel_ignore_build.sh`
# from the repo root on EVERY GitHub-linked deploy (PR previews included),
# before .vercelignore's own exclusions would otherwise matter. Excluding
# either broke every GitHub-triggered deploy with "not a git repository" /
# "No such file or directory" — found live on PR #24 (dpl_FP73Hchne6xUrVLLmZaSr7LyhsbK).
/mac/
/extension/
/site/
/docs/
/evals/
/demo/
/outputs/
/sales/
/data/
/plugins/
/Icarus creatives/
/brag-output-*/
/.github
/.githooks
/.claude
/.codex
/.venv
/.agents
/.worktrees
